---
import SubpageLayout from '../../layouts/SubpageLayout.astro';
---

<SubpageLayout
  title="Security Policy & Vulnerability Disclosure"
  description="Security architecture, credential handling, and responsible vulnerability disclosure procedures."
  status="Official Spec"
  summary="StructZero enforces strict human authorization intercepts, credential masking, and container sandboxing to secure enterprise deployments."
  related={[
    { label: 'Security Controls', href: '/security/' },
    { label: 'Privacy Policy', href: '/legal/privacy/' },
  ]}
>
  <div class="space-y-6">
    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#F5F7FB] mb-2">Vulnerability Management & Code Auditing</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-[#B7C2D6] leading-relaxed">
        Every generated file is audited for security injection risks, hardcoded secrets, and module mismatches prior to repository commit. AST checks confirm imports and type signatures before files are saved.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#F5F7FB] mb-2">Credential Protection & Masking</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-[#B7C2D6] leading-relaxed">
        API keys, access tokens, and sensitive connection strings are automatically sanitized and masked before entering LLM model context windows.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#F5F7FB] mb-2">Sandboxed Execution Runtimes</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-[#B7C2D6] leading-relaxed">
        All build, compilation, and automated test routines take place in isolated, non-root container sandboxes with strictly confined filesystem access.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#F5F7FB] mb-2">Reporting Vulnerabilities</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-[#B7C2D6] leading-relaxed">
        If you discover a potential security vulnerability in StructZero, please report it directly to <code class="text-[#4F8BFF] bg-[#0B1020] px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">security@structzero.app</code>. We investigate all credible reports promptly and practice coordinated disclosure.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</SubpageLayout>
